  "details": "I got a really weird problem. After a couple of minutes my voice cuts out for other players. My microphone is still working, I'm not muted, the volume is all the way up and the microphone symbol flashes when I talk. Its just that people cannot hear me. And it doesn't seem like they can see me talking either (sitation needed).\nI assume its some kind of connection issue since vrchat picks me up talking but does not transmit it to other players.\n\nRestarting VRChat fixes the Issue for a couple of minutes again.\n\nWhat i tried till now:\n-giving the HMD more power\n-trying a different USB-Controller\n-muting and unmuting myself\n-changing microphone volume in VRChat\n-replugging the cable on the HMD\n-replugging the HMD while VRChat is running\nEDIT:\n-using a standard microphone (this completely rules out the oculus or usb being at fault)\n-verify gamefiles via steam\n-reinstalling (with appdata deletion)\n-playing in desktop mode\n\nI've had this issue for a couple of days now. If i find something more out I'll update this post.\n\nAlso im using the Oculus Rift.\n\nEDIT:\nThis might be a big clue I think.\n\nWhile my voice is still transmitting uSpeak outputs this to log:\n[Log:10/1/2017 3:56:40 PM] uSpeak [1344](every 20): Packet latency (152 bytes): combined ping / actual timestamp delta: 145 / 76, ping ours/theirs: 123+-12 / 169+-15\n\n[Log:10/1/2017 3:56:40 PM] uSpeak [1344](every 20): Play voice: estimated latency ms: send delay + transit + buffer = 185, audio length = 60, frame delay = 33.33334, TOTAL = 278.3333\n\nWhen its not working:\n[Log:10/1/2017 4:18:39 PM] uSpeak [1371](every 20): Packet latency (141 bytes): combined ping / actual timestamp delta: 120 / 0, ping ours/theirs: 134+-13 / 106+-9\n\n[Log:10/1/2017 4:18:39 PM] uSpeak [1371](every 20): Play voice: estimated latency ms: send delay + transit + buffer = 0, audio length = 60, frame delay = 33.33334, TOTAL = 93.33334\n\nNotice the \"send delay + transit + buffer\" being equal to 0?\nI'm no audio or network expert, but I do know that most audio related things need a big enough buffer no not distord the sound. And since there is no buffer whatsoever it kinda makes sense to me that it does not work. Of course it says that this is the estimated latency, but I still assume that this is the problem.\nNext question is why it does this and how to fix it.\n\nEDIT:\nOk I just noticed that every now and then the \"send delay + transit + buffer\" is more than 0. (Maybe the mic briefly working again?)\nAlso what I noticed is the \"combined ping / actual timestamp delta:\" part. The combined ping is always showing but the actual timestamp delta is not. So maybe there is some kind off network issue dropping those packages?\n\nHere is the full log: http://puu.sh/xNq3g/2c52bbed73.txt",
